# "As this creature enters, choose a player" and "This creature has protection from the chosen player" are linked (CR
# 607.2d): the second refers only to a choice the first made. Bot1's two True-Name Nemeses both chose Bot2. Mirrorweave makes
# the first a copy of the second until end of turn: the abilities it has now come from that copy effect, and are linked only
# to each other (CR 607.5); they made no choice, so it has protection from no one, and its own choice, made by the text it
# no longer has, is not theirs. Bot2's Lightning Bolt may target it and kills it; the second Nemesis, still protected from
# Bot2, is no target at all.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Pearl
True-Name Nemesis
True-Name Nemesis
Mirrorweave
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.True-Name Nemesis.Cast
Bot1.ChoosePlayer(Bot2)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.True-Name Nemesis.Cast
Bot1.ChoosePlayer(Bot2)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mirrorweave.Cast(True-Name Nemesis#2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(True-Name Nemesis)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Island; Mox Sapphire; Mox Pearl; True-Name Nemesis
Bot1.Battlefield.True-Name Nemesis.ChosenPlayer = 2
Bot1.Graveyard = True-Name Nemesis; Mirrorweave; Black Lotus
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
